  "notes": [
    {
      "claims": [
        "c1"
      ],
      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "limitation",
      "text": "GaussianNB came out higher than the paper (0.586 vs 0.511). On pixel data it is dominated by near-zero-variance background pixels, so it is very sensitive to scikit-learn's var_smoothing and to pixel scaling, neither pinned down by the paper. The tree models, insensitive to both, reproduce (RandomForest) or come close (DecisionTree)."
    }
  ],
